course: dictionary
lesson: 14526
title: Permissible means allowed
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Permissible is a formal word. It means allowed by the rules or by the law. If something is permissible, you are allowed to do it.
explain: «Calculators are permissible in the maths test» means you may use a calculator, because the rules say yes. Everyday speech would say «allowed» or «OK», so you can swap those words in to check the meaning.
explain: Science and safety use it too. «The maximum permissible weight on this lift is 400 kilograms» means 400 kilograms is the most the lift is allowed to carry. Going over that is not permissible.
fact: Permissible means allowed by the rules or by the law.
fact: Permissible also means acceptable.
fact: «Calculators are permissible» means you may use them.
fact: «Maximum permissible weight» means the heaviest load that is allowed.
fact: Everyday words for permissible are allowed and OK.
exercise: «Only pens are permissible in the exam room.» What does permissible mean here? | Hidden away | Broken | Very expensive | *Allowed by the rules
exercise: «The maximum permissible weight on the lift is 400 kilograms.» What does maximum permissible weight mean? | The lightest load you can carry | *The heaviest load that is allowed | The weight of an empty lift
exercise: Priya asks, «Is it permissible to talk during the test?» What is she asking? | Whether she has a test today | Whether talking is fun | *Whether talking is allowed | Whether the teacher can hear her
test: «Running in the corridor is not permissible.» What is the rule? | Running is only allowed at lunch | Running is allowed in the corridor | Running is the fastest way to class | *Running is not allowed in the corridor
test: Ms Hall says, «A cheeky joke is permissible, but keep it kind.» What does permissible mean? | Written down on the board | Very loud | Ruled out for ever | *Acceptable, and fine to do
exam: «A torch is permissible on the camping trip, but a stove is not.» What does permissible mean? | Dangerous to carry | Only for adults | Lost on the trip | *Allowed by the rules
